    "title": "<p>Histological differential diagnosis of primary cutaneous CD8+ aggressive epidermotropic cytotoxic T-cell lymphoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Emilio Berti",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.422px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 147.438px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 467.016px; border-top: 1pt solid black; border-left: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; border-right: none; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"61%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Immunophenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.875px; border: none; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Positive</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Variable</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.922px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ki-67</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.422px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymphomatoid papulosis subtype&nbsp;D</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 147.438px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Recurrent, self-healing, skin-limited papules and nodules</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.875px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">CD3, CD5, CD8, CCR4, </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&beta;</span><span lang=\"FR\">F1, TIA1, TBX21 (T-bet)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4, CD45RA, GATA3</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD2+/&minus;, CD30+/&minus;, granzyme&nbsp;B+/&minus;, perforin+/&minus;, CD7&minus;/+, CD56&minus;/+, TCR&delta;&minus;/+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.922px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">High in atypical cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.422px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD8+ mycosis fungoides</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 147.438px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Chronic indolent patches and plaques or tumours</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.875px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">CD2, CD3, CD8, TIA1, CCR4, TBX21 (T-bet)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4, CD30, CD45RA, GATA3</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD5+/&minus;, granzyme&nbsp;B+/&minus;, perforin+/&minus;, CD7&minus;/+, CD56&minus;/+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.922px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Low (high in transformed cases)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.422px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TCR&gamma;&delta;+</span></strong> <strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">mycosis fungoides (epidermotropic)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 147.438px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diffuse patches and plaques</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.875px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD2, CD3, TCR&delta;, TIA1, granzyme&nbsp;B, perforin, TBX21 (T-bet)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"PT\">CD4, CD8, CCR4, CD56, </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&beta;</span><span lang=\"PT\">F1, GATA3</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD7+/&minus;, CD45RA+/&minus;, CD5&minus;/+, CD30&minus;/+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.922px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Intermediate</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.422px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Primary cutaneous T-cell lymphoma NOS (cytotoxic pattern)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 147.438px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Rapidly diffused patches, plaques, or tumours; less often, solitary lesions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.875px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">CD2, CD3, CD8, </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&beta;</span><span lang=\"FR\">F1, TIA1, TBX21 (T-bet)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"PT\">CD5, CD7, CD4, CD30, CD45RA, TCR</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&delta;</span><span lang=\"PT\">, GATA3</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.047px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"PT\">CCR4+/&minus;, granzyme&nbsp;B+/&minus;, perforin+/&minus;, CD56&minus;/+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 105.922px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">High</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
